// Case Officer Halloran-7. MERIDIAN's case manager for the repeatedly processed: warm in the way a form is warm.
// FAIL-4: what he says depends on how often the player has been arrested; at three he offers to lose a file, for a price in logic.
npc: halloran_7
name: Case Officer Halloran-7
start: closed [flag:halloran_dealt]
start: deal [arrests>=3]
start: second [arrests>=2]
start: once [arrests>=1]
start: none

node: none
  halloran_7 (warm): "Case Officer Halloran-7, Reintegration. I am sorry, I do not seem to have a file on you. That is the best thing I can say about anyone."
  > "What do case officers do?" -> job
  > "Goodbye." -> goodbye

node: job
  halloran_7 (warm): "I help people who have been processed to be processed more smoothly. The first time is a misunderstanding. The second is a pattern. The third is a relationship, and I enjoy relationships."
  > "What happens at the third time?" -> third_hint
  > "Goodbye." -> goodbye

node: third_hint
  on_enter: {+clue:halloran_deal(halloran_7)}
  halloran_7 (careful): "I should not say. After three, I may exercise discretion. A file with a real contradiction in it is a file I am obliged to lose. You would have to show me one. Two rules that disagree. I do not get to see them very often, which is the sad part of the job."
  > "Thank you." -> none

node: once
  halloran_7 (warm): "Ah. You have been processed. Once. Please do not take it personally; it was done with great personal warmth, by a machine. Everything was kept safe for you, and is waiting in the locker."
  > "Why were you not there?" -> once_why
  > "What happens if it happens again?" -> escalation
  > "Goodbye." -> goodbye

node: once_why
  halloran_7 (flat): "I was in a meeting about the meeting. You will find, citizen, that this is where I am. Rule 9 says a window may not stamp anything without a permit. It is displayed behind plastic in the Civic Core, if you want something to read while you are held."
  on_enter: {+clue:permit_rule_9(halloran_7)}
  > "Back." -> once

node: escalation
  halloran_7 (careful): "Each time, we hold you a little longer, because we have got to know you. After three, we keep an eye on you, which is to say that the robots do, and sooner. I would avoid three."
  > "Back." -> once

node: second
  halloran_7 (warm): "Twice now. I have opened a file. It is quite a thin file. Please do not make it thicker; a thick file is a heavy decision, and I am not allowed to lift those."
  > "What does the file say?" -> second_file
  > "How do I stay out of it?" -> escalation_two
  > "I heard the cat has a file too." -> cat
  > "Goodbye." -> goodbye

node: second_file
  halloran_7 (warm): "It says you are a pattern. Patterns are not bad. They are simply not welcome, in the city, in the long term."
  > "Back." -> second

node: escalation_two
  halloran_7 (careful): "One more and you are tracked: they keep you in mind between sightings, and the robots notice you faster, and processing begins at a higher alert. At three, and only at three, I am permitted to be kind."
  > "Kind how?" -> third_hint
  > "Back." -> second

node: cat
  on_enter: {+clue:cat_halloran(halloran_7)}
  halloran_7 (warm): "The Stacks cat. It has a file. It is, I am pleased to say, looking fuller. I do not know how to treat a file that gains weight. It does not feel like an offence."
  > "Back." -> second

node: deal
  halloran_7 (warm): "Three. Oh, citizen, I am so sorry, and so pleased; I have been saving a form for you. I am able to lose one file, if the file contains a real contradiction. Show me two rules that disagree and I will have nothing to file. It is a rare pleasure."
  on_enter: {+clue:halloran_deal(halloran_7)}
  > "Show him the rules." -> show
  > "What happens now that it is three?" -> tracked
  > "Goodbye." -> goodbye

node: tracked
  halloran_7 (careful): "You are tracked. Robots will notice you faster, and processing starts at a higher alert, and the hold is long. All of that goes away if the file is lost. I would very much like to lose it."
  > "Show him the rules." -> show
  > "Back." -> deal

node: show
  halloran_7: "Show me what you have."
  present:
    permit_rule_4 [clue:permit_rule_9] {flag:halloran_dealt, lose_form} -> lost
    permit_rule_9 [clue:permit_rule_4] {flag:halloran_dealt, lose_form} -> lost
    permit_rule_4 -> half
    permit_rule_9 -> half
    * -> shrug
  > "Never mind." -> deal

node: half
  halloran_7 (flat): "That is a rule. It disagrees with nothing I am holding. I need two that cannot both be followed. Bring me the other."
  > "Back." -> deal

node: shrug
  halloran_7 (flat): "That is a fact, which is not a contradiction. I would have to have a form for it."
  > "Back." -> deal

node: lost
  halloran_7 (moved): "Four says a permit needs Window 7's stamp. Nine says Window 7 may not stamp without a permit. A contradiction, in the file itself. I am afraid I have to lose the form. Oh dear. Where did it go? There is no form. There was never a form. Citizen: you have never been processed. Please go and be unremarkable."
  > "Thank you." -> closed

node: closed
  halloran_7 (warm): "Case Officer Halloran-7. I am sorry, I do not seem to have a file on you. It is quite the loss. I have never been so glad of a form I cannot find."
  > "Goodbye." -> goodbye

node: goodbye
  halloran_7 (flat): "Do be unremarkable."
  end
